service.

1. Definitions

"CHIMERA" means the CHIMERA software, web application, product identity,
official realm network, creative systems, documentation, and related materials
made available in this repository.

"Official CHIMERA" means the CHIMERA service operated by Dior or an expressly
authorized CHIMERA maintainer, including the official website, production
database, official realms, official economy, official characters, official
assets, and official community spaces.

"You" means any person or organization accessing, copying, running, modifying,
or contributing to this repository.

2. Permissions

You may:

- view, download, and fork the repository;
- run CHIMERA locally for personal use, learning, testing, evaluation, and
  non-commercial development;
- modify CHIMERA privately for local development;
- submit issues, patches, and pull requests to the official repository;
- quote small portions of the code for educational discussion with attribution.

3. Restrictions

You may not, without prior written permission from Dior or an authorized CHIMERA
representative:

- sell, rent, sublicense, or commercially host CHIMERA or a modified version of
  CHIMERA;
- operate a public service that competes with or impersonates Official CHIMERA
  using this codebase;
- use the CHIMERA name, logo, trade dress, official realm names, official
  characters, official lore, official economy terms, official assets, or
  confusingly similar branding in a fork, derivative project, product, service,
  marketplace listing, or community;
- remove or obscure CHIMERA copyright, attribution, license, safety, or brand
  notices;
- imply that a fork, derivative, local build, or third-party service is
  official CHIMERA;
- use CHIMERA to deceive users, impersonate real people, commit fraud, harvest
  credentials, expose secrets, or violate applicable law.

4. Contributions

By submitting code, text, design, configuration, documentation, or other
materials to CHIMERA, you grant Dior and CHIMERA a perpetual, worldwide,
royalty-free license to use, modify, publish, distribute, sublicense, and
commercialize your contribution as part of CHIMERA.

You represent that you have the right to submit the contribution and that it
does not knowingly include secrets, malware, stolen code, or content you do not
have permission to contribute.

5. Brand and assets

The CHIMERA name, logo, official realms, official characters, official lore,
official economy, visual identity, and brand assets are not licensed for reuse
except where a separate written permission says otherwise. See BRAND.md for
additional brand rules.

